of Forever's look, cut out of the newest export and laid out on one page, so Saneroki can go through them and say
what SaneUI's windows are built from.

  dev/tools/game-art make        cuts the catalogue into assets/generated/game-art (saneui makegameart)
  dev/tools/game-art find WORD   the numbers and atlases whose name holds WORD
  dev/tools/game-art kit         Saneroki's references rebuilt from Forever's pieces into game-art/kit
                                 (saneui makegamekit; game_art_kit.py beside this file)

The page is one of dev/tools/web-pages' (saneui showgameart); overview.pdf beside it is the same numbers on paper, to read
anywhere. A number stays with its piece from round to round (numbers.json beside the page), so a pick said once keeps
meaning the same picture.

Forever's own art is Forever's alone: Retail's build does not hold the c60 sheets. A card says so: "Retail: own look"
when Retail has its own picture under the same name, "Forever only" when it has none.

What it reads:
- the atlases, from the client's tables of the export's build (UiTextureAtlas, UiTextureAtlasMember): a piece's
  sheet, where it lies on it. Forever's own art is the sheets with c60 in their names: the same names as Retail's
  with -c60 added, the larger of the two sizes taken (-2x);
- a sheet the export has no name for lies in sheets/ beside the page by its file ID (the heavy bronze);
- Blizzard's nine-slice layouts (the shared NineSliceLayouts.lua), to put whole windows together;
- the older art that is no atlas (OLD_ART's folders), whole files.
